# 8dp grid

All Compose `dp` values — padding, spacing (`spacedBy`, `Spacer`), sizes, widths, corner radii — are multiples of **8.dp** (Material design grid).

- 4.dp is the only allowed half-step, for tiny gaps inside a component (text-to-text, progress bar thickness).
- Never 2, 3, 6, 10, 12, 14, 20, 22… — round to the nearest multiple of 8 (or 4 for tiny gaps).

```kotlin
// ❌
Modifier.padding(horizontal = 12.dp, vertical = 10.dp).width(380.dp)
// ✅
Modifier.padding(horizontal = 16.dp, vertical = 8.dp).width(384.dp)
```

When touching an existing file, fix off-grid values in the code you change.
